{
  "id": "vlc",
  "name": "VLC media player",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Video",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "vlc.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "org.videolan.vlc"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://wiki.videolan.org/QtHotkeys/"
  ],
  "note": "The VideoLAN wiki's Hotkeys table documents a single set of hotkeys for the Qt interface (Windows and Linux); it does not publish a separate macOS column, so no 'mac' chord is included here (VLC's native macOS build uses its own Cocoa menu shortcuts, which are not covered by this table). Skipped as not expressible by the chord grammar: 'Navigate menus (DVD)' (bound to the generic 'Arrows', not a specific key), 'Scale down/up subtitles text' (Ctrl+Mouse wheel, a scroll gesture), and 'History back' (the wiki table itself flags this row 'Please check this' as unverified).",
